      "short_description": "Bowdoin College is a private, coeducational liberal arts college located in Brunswick, Maine. Founded in 1794, it is one of the oldest institutions of higher education in the state. The college offers an undergraduate liberal arts curriculum that emphasizes rigorous intellectual engagement and provides students with flexibility in course selection.\n\nBowdoin has approximately 1,500 enrolled students and cosponsors study-abroad programs in various locations, including Rome and Sri Lanka. The campus features notable facilities such as the Peary-MacMillan Arctic Museum, the Hawthorne-Longfellow Library, and the Bowdoin Scientific Station. Historic buildings, like the Walker Art Building, add to the college's rich architectural heritage.\n\nThe college has a distinguished list of alumni, including U.S. President Franklin Pierce and renowned figures like Nathaniel Hawthorne and Henry Wadsworth Longfellow. Bowdoin College continues to foster a vibrant academic community dedicated to the liberal arts.",
